\title{doobr: Nonparametric Simulation of Future Sample Paths for Scenario Generation}
\description{
Generates future sample paths and scenario trees for a univariate time series without assuming a parametric data generating process. Any learner may supply the conditional mean and conditional scale; the innovations are resampled from an honest bank of out-of-fold standardised residuals obtained by purged K-fold cross-fitting, so that the simulated increments form a martingale difference sequence rather than inheriting the optimism of in-sample residuals. Provides martingale-difference tests for both estimation steps and calibration tests for the simulated paths.
}
